{
  "passages": [
    {
      "block_id": "P2-S09-p01",
      "doc_id": "P2",
      "snapshot": "published",
      "heading": "Rule 8: Share and explain your data",
      "sentence_index": [
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0001",
          "text": "Having access to a clearly annotated notebook is of little use to those wanting to reproduce or extend your results if the underlying data are locked away. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0002",
          "text": "Strive to make your data or a sample of your data publicly available along with the notebook. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0003",
          "text": "While sharing your data takes careful planning, notebooks make it easy to provide a description of your input data and upstream processing steps, which are essential for interpreting results."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P2-S09-p02",
      "doc_id": "P2",
      "snapshot": "published",
      "heading": "Rule 8: Share and explain your data",
      "sentence_index": [
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0004",
          "text": "Ideally, you will share your entire data set alongside your notebooks. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0005",
          "text": "We realize many data sets are too large or too sensitive to share this way. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0006",
          "text": "In these cases, consider breaking down large and complex data sets into tiers such that, even if the raw data are prohibitively large to include alongside your published notebooks or are constrained by privacy or other access issues, reproducibility and interpretability isn’t lost. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0007",
          "text": "You can host public copies of medium-sized, anonymized data in a variety of hosting services (for example, figshare [ https://figshare.com/ ], zenodo [ https://zenodo.org/ ]), and include further processed data sets alongside the notebooks in the final repository. "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0008",
          "text": "To uniquely and permanently identify data sets, these hosting services provide Digital Object Identifiers (dois). "
        },
        {
          "sentence_id": "sent-0009",
          "text": "This tiered approach both provides public confidence and allows others to reproduce and reuse the latter stages of an analysis even without access to the full, raw data set."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "claim": "在原始数据受大小或隐私约束时，作者提出分层共享的办法，使他人在未取得完整原始数据的情况下仍有机会复用分析的后续阶段。"
}

